          "overall_reasoning": "These columns are PCoA ordination coordinates from beta diversity on 16S ASVs. The guideline allows \u00b10.05 absolute error per axis and lets each axis flip sign. Sign is arbitrary in PCoA, so compare_abs=true covers those flips. This is looser than checking for one global flip per axis, but it is acceptable. The comparison only supports relative error, not absolute. Typical coordinate values are about 0.1\u20130.4, so a \u00b10.05 error is roughly 15\u201340% relative. I set a cell tolerance of 0.3 as a reasonable stand-in. The first five axes hold most of the explained variance and are stable between the two files: Axis.1\u20133 match closely, and Axis.4\u20135 match after a sign flip. These are compared. Higher axes (6\u201324) explain very little variance and are numerically unstable. Their order and values shift with small changes in how the data is processed (e.g. Axis.15\u201316 differ substantially even after sign flips). They also contain many values near zero, where relative error blows up. So they are ignored. The candidate's extra 'group' column has no counterpart in the reference and is not compared.",
